title: mf duplicate trash
tags: [[CLI command]] Duplicates
kind: reference
summary: Trash the copies a query matches, where a twin exists outside it

In every group with a copy outside the query, every copy matching it goes to the
trash; a group wholly inside the query is left alone. The copies to trash are the
query `Q AND same(mfr_duplicate_group, NOT Q)`: each has a twin outside `Q` that the
run leaves, so no group loses its last copy ([[Deleting duplicate copies]]).

```
mf duplicate trash 'mfr_path ->* "/downloads"'
```

It is <<cmd "mf duplicate keep">> of the complement — `keep 'NOT (Q)'` trashes the
same copies — spelled for the case where the query at hand names what to give up:
a folder to empty of what is kept elsewhere, or the folder a list shows
([[mf:duplicate]]). Listing, confirmation, `--dry-run` and a failure mid-run are as
for `keep`.
